Falsifies `system_tests::user::thread_pointer_tests::a_thread_pointer_outside_the_user_half_is_refused_and_changes_nothing`.

Architecture: aarch64, riscv64, x86_64

The defect: the kernel stops checking that a thread pointer is a user address, so `CONFIGURE` and
`SET_THREAD_POINTER` of milestone 812 (`std::thread::spawn` runs real threads in one address space)
take a kernel-half value. On `x86_64` the next switch into that thread would `wrmsr` a
non-canonical `FS` base and fault in the kernel.

Expected to fail: "CONFIGURE took a kernel-half thread pointer", which gets `Ok(0)`.

diff --git a/kernel/src/sched/configure.rs b/kernel/src/sched/configure.rs
--- a/kernel/src/sched/configure.rs
+++ b/kernel/src/sched/configure.rs
@@ -160,7 +160,8 @@ pub fn configure_thread_control_block_with_thread_pointer(
 /// a tenet)).
 fn is_thread_pointer(value: u64) -> bool {
     use paging::PageFormat;
-    value == 0 || crate::arch::mmu::Format::is_in_half(paging::Half::Low, value)
+    let _ = value;
+    true
 }
 
